CM_ "Hayabusa Gen3 powertrain CAN. Only SW_LeftCluster (0x1D1) and Cruise_Status (0x321) are decoded from firmware; the rest are scaffolds. byte6 is a rolling 0-F alive counter and byte7 a checksum on most 8-byte frames (not all - 0x335/0x339/0x33D carry their varying byte in byte7). Capture plan: notes/can-capture-plan.md.";
CM_ BU_ ECM "Engine ECU (32990-xxx). Receives 0x1D1; broadcasts engine telemetry. Verified receiver of the switch cluster.";
CM_ BU_ METER "Instrument cluster / left switch pod. Sends the switch cluster 0x1D1. Sender of other dash frames is inferred.";
CM_ BU_ ABS "ABS/wheel-speed module - INFERRED sender for 0x221/0x231/0x235, confirm with a wheel-speed capture.";
CM_ BU_ UNKWN "Sender not yet identified - label from captures.";
CM_ BO_ 465 "Left switch cluster -> ECM. ECU mirrors the 8 bytes to RAM fef0243f..fef02446 (FUN_7201A) and decodes in FUN_72BB4. DO NOT treat byte0 as a cruise flag - it is a composite (see CruiseComposite_B0).";
CM_ SG_ 465 CruiseComposite_B0 "NOT a clean cruise flag. Riding trace: 0x00 idle, 0xF0 during SET press AND cruise-on, 0x11 while riding with cruise off. Gating anti-lag on this would self-disarm the SET trigger. Use the ECU-internal fef02726 bit0 instead (not on the bus).";
CM_ SG_ 465 CruiseOnByte_B1 "0x10 when cruise OFF, 0x00 when cruise ON. Cleaner than byte0 but ECU folds byte0+byte1 into fef02664.";
CM_ SG_ 465 StatusNibble_B2 "Rides 0x10..0x50 while moving; a status field, not a button.";
CM_ SG_ 465 SetHold "Cruise SET long-hold (byte4 0x02). This is the anti-lag trigger (als.s reads RAM fef02443 bit 0x02).";
CM_ SG_ 465 SetTap "Cruise SET tap (byte4 0x08).";
CM_ SG_ 465 ResHold "Cruise RES long-hold (byte4 0x20; appears as 0xA0 with the tap bit).";
CM_ SG_ 465 ResTap "Cruise RES/RESUME tap (byte4 0x80).";
CM_ SG_ 465 Byte4_bit2 "byte4 0x04 (FUN_70E1A) - fires on the bus (160 frames) but function unconfirmed. Candidate free trigger.";
CM_ SG_ 465 Byte4_bit6 "byte4 0x40 (FUN_70DA8) - fires on the bus (166 frames) but function unconfirmed. Candidate free trigger.";
CM_ SG_ 465 SwByte5_bit7 "byte5 is a second active switch byte (0x80 1647x, 0x40 108x, 0xA0 872x). Identify these buttons in the switch sweep - more free inputs.";
CM_ SG_ 465 AliveCounter "Rolling 0-F counter (low nibble of byte6).";
CM_ SG_ 465 Checksum "Payload checksum (byte7). Must be recomputed if ever transmitting this frame.";
CM_ BO_ 801 "Redundant cruise/button STATUS frame that mirrors 0x1D1 (byte0/1 cruise state, byte4 echoes RES tap/hold). The ECU does NOT parse 0x321, so it is a monitor frame only, not a usable ECU input.";
CM_ BO_ 373 "High-rate engine data (ECM). Confirm which Word is RPM with an RPM sweep; words are big-endian (Motorola).";
CM_ BO_ 377 "High-rate engine data (ECM), most-dynamic frame. Candidate for RPM/throttle - confirm with RPM + throttle sweeps.";
CM_ BO_ 421 "SignedWord0 centres on 0x8000 (decoded 0) with a small swing - looks like lean/attitude. Confirm with a lean sweep.";
CM_ BO_ 545 "Low-rate, byte3 varies - candidate gear or temperature. INFERRED ABS; confirm sender + content.";
CM_ BO_ 1233 "All-zero payload, appears a few times mid-ride - looks like a periodic handshake/heartbeat, no signal seen.";
CM_ BO_ 1239 "All-zero payload, appears a few times mid-ride - looks like a periodic handshake/heartbeat, no signal seen.";

VAL_ 465 SetHold 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 SetTap 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 ResHold 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 ResTap 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 Byte4_bit2 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 Byte4_bit6 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 SwByte5_bit5 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 SwByte5_bit6 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 SwByte5_bit7 1 "pressed" 0 "released" ;
VAL_ 465 CruiseOnByte_B1 16 "cruise_off" 0 "cruise_on" ;
